{
 "encounter_id": "00697",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Morning. I'm not here for a lecture. I had COVID in March, and I'm still not right, six months on."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "No lecture. Tell me how you're not right."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Tired. Not normal tired, flat. I wake up tired. I was running a team of twelve and now I can't concentrate on an email."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Anything else?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Breathless on the stairs, and when I walk quickly. I get a tight feeling in my chest, but no pain."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any chest pain at all?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, I said, it's tightness, not pain. No chest pain."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Fair, thank you. What are you taking at the moment?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Vitamin D, 1000 units, every day, which I forget about half the time. That's all."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Okay, so the plan is daily, but you often forget. Any long-term conditions?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Type 2 diabetes, diet-controlled."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any lung problems in the family?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "My mum had COPD. She smoked."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And do you smoke?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Never. Not once."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check you. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 82, blood pressure 128 over 80, temperature 36.7, oxygen 97 percent, and weight 79 kilos.",
   "pause": 12.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "All right? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "All fine at rest. Take a deep breath in for me, and out.",
   "pause": 18.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I've been told my chest is clear before. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "It's clear again today, no wheeze at all."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "So what is this? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "After COVID, many people have fatigue and breathlessness for months. That's what's commonly called long COVID. But I can't rule out asthma coming on after the infection, because of the chest tightness."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Can you do something? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to arrange a breathing test, spirometry, to see how your lungs behave."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. And treatment? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "In the meantime, I'm going to give you a salbutamol inhaler, 100 micrograms, two puffs when you're tight or breathless, and we'll see if it helps."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fair. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pace yourself, short breaks during the day, build up activity slowly, and don't push on the bad days."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's hard in my job. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I know. If your employer allows a phased return, even better. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "What if it doesn't improve? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "If your breathlessness is no better in four weeks, come back and see me and we'll look at other tests."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. Thanks. ~"
  }
 ],
